<CONSTRAINTS>
#1305: NEVER work in /root/ on rental boxes. ALL file operations (tar extract, build, source upload) MUST go to a subdirectory (e.g. /root/ninfer/). Working in /root/ clobbers .ssh/authorized_keys and kills SSH access. This has caused box destruction at least twice.
#2337: The Windows box (n1nj4@station.hq.pe): serve lifecycle belongs to the owner, exclusively. The agent must NEVER run process-lifecycle commands (taskkill, Stop-Process, starting bats, killing PIDs) against the box — even when own tool output appears to contradict the owner's statement about what is running; the owner's account wins. Allowed scope: read logs, stage/verify files, gate boots by reading banners. This rule exists because an unrequested `taskkill /F` on the serving endpoint (2026-10-28) took down the serve while the agent argued with the owner's correct restart claim — and the endpoint also carries the agent's own inference channel.
#2402: station.hq.pe is a self-hosting box: the Infernix daily serve on it generates this agent's own tokens. NEVER launch a second full-model engine process (perplexity/serve/bench boot — validation and preflight boots included) on it while the serve is up, without an owner-opened window per run; a prior go for one boot is not blanket approval. Violated 2026-10-29: co-run perplexity boots OOM-killed the daily serve (VRAM headroom ~775 MiB, PID 6664→63120). Measurement batteries run only after the owner stops the serve and says GO, or on a rental.
#2433: This agent's own model inference runs ON station.hq.pe (model id station/qwen3.8-flash-next on the daily infernix-serve) — the box it operates is its own runtime host, and the serve is load-bearing for the whole agent ecosystem; it cannot be scheduled down for agent work. Rules that follow: (1) memory/footprint problems are AUTHORING-TIME facts — resident bytes are derivable from code + artifact descriptor constants by inspection before any run; a runtime OOM that surprises us means the code was never read against the budget, and if prior design work (e.g. argon walls) already banked the arithmetic, the implementation must be diffed against those numbers before acceptance. (2) SEPARATE-PROCESS GPU workloads (torch replica-class: their own weight copies, their own allocator, no cooperation with the resident serve) cannot coexist on the 32 GB card — serve ~26 GB resident, caps abort only after spill/TDR damage; precedent: 2026-10-30 Window A driver resets from unbounded caches whose 100 GB+ sum was readable in the source; 2026-10-29 co-run OOM killed the serve. This ban is on the separate-process SHAPE, not on training work per se: engine-native work inside the serve (idle-cycle slices, resident-weight reuse, quiescence gates) is the owner-required product path for PLE graft descent (see #2406) and is judged by measured live-traffic impact, not excluded by the coexistence arithmetic.
#2435: The agent's model inference runs on station.hq.pe (the daily infernix-serve, qwen3.8-flash-next) — the box it operates is its own runtime host, and the serve is load-bearing for the whole agent ecosystem. GPU work risking VRAM spill cannot run there: resident serve ~26 GB + desktop ~1 GB leaves no headroom for descent-class work (~20 GB floor) on a 32 GB card, and allocation transients race the serve for the same memory.
#2476: qudata rentals: ALWAYS rent with the proven template id 68fa3b8efe83b162bd8b2f86 ("Hashcat CUDA", dizcza/docker-hashcat — CUDA base, ssh verified working). NEVER select a custom ninfer-* template (6ab86d44…, 6ab82f62…) however fitting the image name — custom nvidia/cuda-based template booted with ssh_enabled=False/tunnel_host=None twice (7.52 precedent, 2026-10-31 8×V100 box, 9.85 R burned); a template's `ssh=True` metadata flag does NOT mean the runtime container serves ssh. User has flagged this forgetting pattern repeatedly.
